<p>NOTE: For the first nine months of 1996, the company had a weighted average of 52,755,536 shares outstanding compared with a weighted average of 49,388,896 shares outstanding in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>Current quarter includes results of the defense electronics and systems business of Westinghouse, which Northrop acquired on March 1 and operates as its Electronic Sensors and Systems Division. Comparative results for 1995 do not include ESSD data.</p>
<p>Net income for Q3 included a $6 million pretax gain from the sale of stock owned in ETEC Systems Inc.</p>
<p>Q3 operating profit included the disposition of three claims stemming from work performed in the 1980's.  The military and commercial aircraft segment benefited $31 million from the settlement of two claims while the electronics business segment operating profit was reduced by $29 million as the result of the writedown of a claim related to avionics work performed by the former Grumman Corp prior to its acquisition by Northrop in 1994.</p>
